{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Six days you shall labor and do all your work</b> The meaning of עֲבוֹדָה (labor) is work that is not for the bodily enjoyment, such as food for oneself and the like, as in the expressions that are said: \"and in all manner of service in the field\" (Exodus 1:14), \"when you work the ground\" (Genesis 4:12), \"and you shall work it and sow it\" (Ezekiel 36:9), and as I will yet explain, with Elohim's help (Leviticus 23:7). And therefore it says <b>six days you shall labor</b> the ground, <b>and you shall do all your work</b>, which is for the need of your body and for your enjoyment, as in the matter of \"that which you will bake, bake\" (Exodus 16:23), and on the Sabbath you shall not do any work. <b>You, and your son, and your daughter</b> — the young ones: He warned us concerning the Sabbath that the young children shall not do work with our knowledge and by our will (Shabbat 121a). <b>And your male servant and your female servant</b> — the slaves who were circumcised and immersed, who are obligated in all the laws of the Sabbath like an Israelite, as He said in Mishneh Torah (Deuteronomy 5:14), \"so that your male servant and your female servant may rest as well as you.\" And these are obligated in all the commandments like women, as is explained in the words of our Sages (Ḥagigah 4a), and it would have been fitting to warn them themselves, for they themselves are commanded in the Sabbath, but the verse speaks together with us because the slaves are in our domain, to say that their rest is upon us, and if we do not restrain them, we are punished for them. Furthermore, because Elohim addresses all of Israel in all Ten Commandments:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:17:23.941679961Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}